{
 "schemaVersion": 1,
 "id": "kukhnya-s01e18-scene-13",
 "pair": "ru-en",
 "title": "Отравился  (Poisoned)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "fedya": "Федя",
  "senya": "Сеня"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Senya is lying in the staff room looking terrible after eating fish that was past its best, and Fedya is trying to help. His remedy is not a very medical one. Listen for the moment it all goes wrong.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Ты выглядишь совсем плохо.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "У тебя болит живот?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Да, мне очень плохо.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Я же тебе говорил.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Не надо было есть рыбу.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Я думал, она нормальная.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Знаешь, что надо делать?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Надо выпить перец и воду.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Ой, я больше не могу.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Сеня, что с тобой?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Сеня, открой глаза! Сеня!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Сеня, держись!",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Back to the staff room, slowly.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Ты выглядишь совсем плохо.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You look really bad.' \"Vyglyadish\", you look, is \"glyadet\", to look, with \"vy-\", out, in front.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "У тебя болит живот?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Does your stomach hurt?' \"U tebya bolit zhivot?\", 'at you hurts belly': the belly does the hurting.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Да, мне очень плохо.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yes, I feel really bad.' \"Mne plokho\" can also mean I feel sick or faint, not just unhappy.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Я же тебе говорил.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I told you so.' \"Govoril\" rather than \"skazal\": it simply states that the warning was given.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Не надо было есть рыбу.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You shouldn't have eaten the fish.' \"Ne nado bylo\", 'not needed it was'. \"Bylo\", was, puts the whole thing in the past.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Я думал, она нормальная.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I thought it was fine.' \"Ona\", she, stands for the fish, since \"ryba\" is feminine. \"Normalnaya\" here just means okay.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Знаешь, что надо делать?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Do you know what to do?' \"Znaesh?\", you know?, becomes a question just by the voice going up. \"Delat\" is to do.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Надо выпить перец и воду.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You need to drink pepper and water.' \"Voda\", water, becomes \"vodu\" as the thing you drink. \"Perets\", pepper, stays as it is.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Ой, я больше не могу.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Oh, I can't take any more.' \"Bolshe ne mogu\", 'more not I can': I can't go on.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Сеня, что с тобой?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Senya, what's wrong with you?' \"Chto s toboy?\", 'what with you?', is how you ask what's the matter.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Сеня, открой глаза! Сеня!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Senya, open your eyes!' \"Otkroy\", open!, is said to one person. One eye is \"glaz\"; two are \"glaza\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Сеня, держись!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Senya, hold on!' \"Derzhis\" is \"derzhat\", to hold, with \"-sya\": 'hold yourself'. You can say it to anyone struggling. And now the scene at full speed once more.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Ты выглядишь совсем плохо.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "У тебя болит живот?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Да, мне очень плохо.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Я же тебе говорил.",
   "gap": 0.5
